{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/69517-using-mythology-in-hunter","id":69517,"title":"Using mythology in Hunter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-10T17:45:53-08:00","id":69517,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Using mythology in Hunter","content":"One of the things I find fascinating with Hunter is that the fluff in each book looks backwards and intertwines mythology and the lore of World of Darkness. This is something I'm interested in exploring in a campaign I'm running. I'm rather taken with the idea that things that inspired, took inspiration from or are actively masquerading as ancient deities and monsters are still running around and peddling influence in the modern world, albeit in a somewhat subtler way. To that end, I'm interested in compiling some sources to look at, both from various WoD lines and original conspiracy theories, about what mythological personae were what type of WoD creature. I know that there may be multiple viable theories as without even doing a lot of hardcore research, I've mentally considered that &quot;gods&quot; may be anything from an unlikely alliance of mixed races (Mages, Vampires, Werewolves etc. working together), that the originals might have been all of one type of creature or another (all Mages or all Werewolves etc.) but other creatures have borrowed the legend or been mistaken for the originals (such as a Werewolf claiming the name Anubis who was originally a Sin Eater.) I'm curious as to what hints have been dropped in the books and fan theories.<br /> <br /> In particular my focus is on the Olympians but I rather like the idea that other pantheons are not controlling various conspiracies outright but are steering them towards or away from their interests in small, tactical ways (as opposed to outright dictating dogma and strategy, which seems unlikely to fly for any meaningful length of time if the dogma and strategies are too out of line with the founding principles of the conspiracy or the beliefs of the rank and file.) For example I could see the Egyptians and various other near eastern and north African remnants having a stake in the Ascending Ones or Aegis Kai Doru being a successor to ancient heroes who came to despise monstrous &quot;false gods&quot; and the god like sorcerer kings. One idea I had was that in the waning days of Rome following the establishment of Christianity as the Empire's official religion, a group of priests who kept the old faiths decided to try to win back their followers by bringing back the gods, trying to summon them into earthly vessels made from members of the Empire's elite families who used to claim they could trace their lineage back to the gods themselves.... It worked. Sort of....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T10:44:31-08:00","id":70692,"title":"","content":"I normally go with the idea that the classic Gods really were as powerful as the myths said and are still around today, not hugely active but when they are you want to be very careful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T13:03:29-08:00","id":70801,"title":"","content":"Book of the Dead has a dominion in the Underworld which is ruled by a couple who have more than a passing resemblance to Hades and Persephone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T18:57:31-08:00","id":70967,"title":"","content":"The assumption that most of the old stories are mostly literal accounts is a fun one. I'm fascinated by many takes on it whether it be mistaken identity like a Promethean using the legend of Ares and being rolled into it (Ares is barely mentioned in Greek mythology and despised by most gods and mortals when he does appear, justifiably so as he's a coward and psychopath by all accounts but what if that was Torment and propaganda? Mars on the other hand barely resembles his Greek predecessor and thus leads me to conclude the god himself matured or someone else is starring as Mars rather than the guy everyone hates (either because he was in defiance of the natural order or just a bloody minded loon.) So I'm hoping anyone can steer me towards similar uses of mythology as in the Vigil fiction or their own pet theories about who was what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}